// Regression: a tuplet in ONE voice must not reach another voice's beaming.
// Voice 1 has a quarter-note triplet (its "3" bracket sits above); voice 2 has
// eight straight eighths that must beam 4+4 (two half-measure groups), below,
// stems down. The detector once shared score.TupletBrackets across every voice,
// so voice 1's triplet end-index split voice 2's first group into [e' f'] + two
// stray flags; tuplets now carry a VoiceIndex and the detector filters by it.
// ⚠️ The rule that made that reachable — "a beam ends at a tuplet boundary" — was
// an invention and is gone (2026-07-31); what the filter still feeds is the
// beamlet clamp at a tuplet's own ends. The grouping here is answered by voice 2's
// own durations against 4/4's beamExceptions, and the book holds it there.
// LILYPOND-REF: lily/auto-beam-engraver.cc — beaming is per Voice.
octave absolute
title "Multi-voice tuplet + beams"
part mel { clef treble }
section S {
  mel {
    voice { tuplet 3/2 { c''4 c'' c'' } c''2 | }
    voice { e'8 f' g' a' b' a' g' f' | }
  }
}
form main { S }
score main "multivoice-tuplet-beams" { staff mel }
